Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on practicing Express.js concepts through basic coding examples. Simple server setups were implemented to understand routing, middleware usage, and handling HTTP requests. Small examples were created to observe how different routes respond to client requests. This hands-on practice helped in connecting theoretical concepts with real implementation.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was improved confidence in building basic backend functionality using Express.js. The practice strengthened understanding of routing and request-response handling. It also enhanced the ability to structure simple APIs effectively. Overall, the session contributed to better practical knowledge of Express.js development.
